WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.867 --> 00:00:07.460
King Midas was a very kind man.

2
00:00:07.461 --> 00:00:11.551
He loved to listen to music and eat delicious food.

3
00:00:11.552 --> 00:00:14.976
He also loved strolling in his rose garden.

4
00:00:14.977 --> 00:00:19.580
One evening a satyr named Silenus got lost.

5
00:00:19.581 --> 00:00:25.085
He wandered into King Midas' rose garden and soon fell asleep.

6
00:00:25.086 --> 00:00:32.988
The next morning King Midas' gardener found the satyr in the garden and took him to the king.

7
00:00:32.989 --> 00:00:35.772
Silenus stood before King Midas.

8
00:00:35.773 --> 00:00:40.760
"Why were you sleeping in my rose garden?" asked the king.

9
00:00:40.761 --> 00:00:47.568
Silenus explained how he had gotten lost, and King Midas felt sorry for the creature.

10
00:00:47.569 --> 00:00:52.500
"I will not punish you. You may go in peace," he said.

11
00:00:52.501 --> 00:00:56.386
Silenus was very grateful to King Midas.

12
00:00:56.387 --> 00:01:01.179
Silenus was an old friend of Dionysus, the god of wine.

13
00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:04.160
Dionysus was very powerful.

14
00:01:04.161 --> 00:01:09.338
He listened as Silenus told him about the kind King Midas.

15
00:01:09.339 --> 00:01:14.332
After hearing the story, Dionysus went to see King Midas.

16
00:01:14.333 --> 00:01:18.012
He wanted to reward him with a special gift.

17
00:01:18.013 --> 00:01:21.929
"You were kind to my friend. So I will give you one wish.

18
00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:28.055
You may have whatever you want," said Dionysus.

19
00:01:28.056 --> 00:01:31.646
The king did not have to think for very long.

20
00:01:31.647 --> 00:01:33.960
He knew exactly what he wanted.

21
00:01:33.961 --> 00:01:45.883
"I wish that everything I touch will turn to gold!" said the excited king.

22
00:01:45.884 --> 00:01:48.895
Then he picked up a stone from the ground.

23
00:01:48.896 --> 00:01:54.896
King Midas stared at the gold stone in his hand. His wish had come true!

24
00:01:54.897 --> 00:01:58.779
King Midas touched the door. He touched the throne.

25
00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:02.256
He ran over and touched the table.

26
00:02:02.257 --> 00:02:07.294
"I'm rich! I'm the richest man in the world!" shouted the happy king.

27
00:02:07.295 --> 00:02:13.852
King Midas had fun turning his possessions into gold, but before long, he was hungry.

28
00:02:13.853 --> 00:02:17.091
"Bring me my dinner!" boomed the king.

29
00:02:17.092 --> 00:02:20.739
The servant brought in a large dish of chicken.

30
00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:25.170
But when Midas picked up the chicken and bit it, what happened?

31
00:02:25.171 --> 00:02:29.211
Ouch! It turned to gold!

32
00:02:29.212 --> 00:02:34.246
The king was so hungry, but everything he touched turned to gold.

33
00:02:34.247 --> 00:02:38.354
How could he eat gold? It was not possible.

34
00:02:38.355 --> 00:02:42.192
The frustrated and hungry king needed some fresh air.

35
00:02:42.193 --> 00:02:47.427
The rose garden was the only place where King Midas could find peace.

36
00:02:47.428 --> 00:02:50.719
He reached out to smell one of the roses.

37
00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:56.014
When he touched the rose, it turned into gold and fell to the ground.

38
00:02:56.015 --> 00:03:02.300
As the king tried to run away, he bumped into the bushes and turned them all into gold.

39
00:03:02.301 --> 00:03:06.589
"Oh, my beautiful roses!" cried the king.

40
00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:10.259
King Midas was not enjoying himself anymore.

41
00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:13.706
The king was getting tired and wanted to rest.

42
00:03:13.707 --> 00:03:18.407
He laid his head on his pillow, but it turned to gold as well.

43
00:03:18.408 --> 00:03:24.249
"Why? Why did I make this wish?" cried the king.

44
00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:27.813
King Midas was the richest man in the world.

45
00:03:27.814 --> 00:03:32.625
He got exactly what he asked for: everything he touched turned to gold.

46
00:03:32.626 --> 00:03:37.706
But he was not happy. In fact, he was miserable.

47
00:03:37.707 --> 00:03:42.109
He could not eat, sleep, or admire his flowers.

48
00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:48.189
Then King Midas heard the royal trumpets. "At last!" shouted the king.

49
00:03:48.190 --> 00:03:53.007
"Here is someone who can make me happy again!"

50
00:03:53.008 --> 00:03:57.367
The king ran and opened the gold door to welcome his daughter.

51
00:03:57.368 --> 00:04:01.055
She had just returned from a long journey.

52
00:04:01.056 --> 00:04:04.592
"Father!" the princess shouted happily.

53
00:04:04.593 --> 00:04:07.608
"My daughter!" shouted the king.

54
00:04:07.609 --> 00:04:13.670
But as soon as King Midas touched the princess, she turned into a gold statue.

55
00:04:13.671 --> 00:04:19.722
"No! No! This must end!" cried the king.

56
00:04:19.723 --> 00:04:24.046
That evening Dionysus received an unexpected visit.

57
00:04:24.047 --> 00:04:29.654
"Please, I don't want the golden touch anymore," King Midas said sadly.

58
00:04:29.655 --> 00:04:33.149
"I thought you wanted to be rich," said Dionysus.

59
00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:37.474
"No amount of gold is worth losing the things I love."

60
00:04:37.475 --> 00:04:40.506
Dionysus felt sorry for Midas.

61
00:04:40.507 --> 00:04:45.077
"I wish I had never asked for this gift," Midas said.

62
00:04:45.078 --> 00:04:49.475
"I'm glad you learned a lesson from this," Dionysus told the king.

63
00:04:49.476 --> 00:04:51.766
"I will grant you your new wish."

64
00:04:51.767 --> 00:04:56.249
Everything the king had touched returned to normal.

65
00:04:56.250 --> 00:05:00.801
King Midas was so happy to have all his things restored.

66
00:05:00.802 --> 00:05:04.760
Most of all, he was happy to have his daughter back.

67
00:05:04.761 --> 00:05:09.500
King Midas was not as rich as before, but it didn't matter.

68
00:05:09.501 --> 00:05:17.392
For he learned that the best things in life are not made of gold.
